data_tis2
# Phase identity: cxr-mc crystal catalog entry [tis2].
# Bundled full-basis P1 CIF used by the declarative material catalog.
# Catalog provenance and assumptions:
# 1T (CdI2-type, P-3m1) metal dichalcogenides: heavy metal on Wyckoff 1a (0,0,0)
# -- AT THE ORIGIN, so every (00l) stays strong (unlike the 2H TMDs where the
# metal at z=1/4,3/4 makes them oscillate) -- and chalcogen on 2d (1/3,2/3,z),
# (2/3,1/3,1-z) with z ~ 0.255. One layer per cell, so c is the interlayer
# repeat. Bond sqrt((a/sqrt(3))^2 + (z c)^2) ~ 2.5 A.
# 1T-TiS2, CdI2-type P-3m1: one TiS2 formula unit, Ti on 1a and S on 2d.
# a=3.407 A, c=5.695 A, S z=0.2493: Brown et al., Phys. Rev. B 57, 5101
# (1998), doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.57.5101. Assumes a stoichiometric ambient
# 1T cell. Limiting checks: V=(sqrt(3)/2)a^2c, 1Ti+2S, and a finite (003)
# coupling; the 1T metal at the origin leaves the requested odd basal order allowed.
# Validation: tis2-003-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
_cell_length_a 3.407
_cell_length_b 3.407
_cell_length_c 5.695
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 120.0
